<title>JAPAN: Aramco sets Feb propane at $320/T, butane $305/T.</title>
<headline>Aramco sets Feb propane at $320/T, butane $305/T.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia's state-owned oil firm Saudi Aramco said on Thursday it had lowered its propane contract price for February by $10 from the previous month to $320 per tonne, and its price for butane by $25 to $305 per tonne.  </p>
<p>The propane price for February is up $115 from a year ago, while butane is up $117 over the same period.</p>
<p>The Saudi contract price is loosely based on the results of three monthly spot tenders and the company's own assessment of spot market trends.</p>
</text>
